# NOTICE

## Upstream project

This repository is a **Windows port** of
[bosectl](https://github.com/aaronsb/bosectl) by **Aaron Bockelie**,
distributed under the MIT License.

The BMAP reverse-engineering work — the protocol framing, the register
addresses, the per-model quirks, the device catalog — is entirely upstream's
work. This port only changes *how bytes reach the headphones on Windows*, plus
the user interface around it.

### Files copied essentially verbatim from upstream

These files are taken from upstream and kept as close to identical as the
line-ending policy allows, so that a diff against upstream stays meaningful
and future upstream fixes can be merged by inspection:

| This repository | Upstream path |
| --- | --- |
| `pybmap/protocol.py` | `python/pybmap/protocol.py` |
| `pybmap/constants.py` | `python/pybmap/constants.py` |
| `pybmap/types.py` | `python/pybmap/types.py` |
| `pybmap/errors.py` | `python/pybmap/errors.py` |
| `pybmap/catalog.py` | `python/pybmap/catalog.py` |
| `pybmap/connection.py` | `python/pybmap/connection.py` |
| `pybmap/cli.py` | `python/pybmap/cli.py` |
| `pybmap/devices/` (all modules) | `python/pybmap/devices/` |
| `fixtures/packets/` | `fixtures/packets/` |
| `tests/test_*.py` (most) | `python/tests/test_*.py` |

The upstream release this port tracks is recorded in
`pybmap.UPSTREAM_VERSION`.

### Files written for this port

| Path | What changed and why |
| --- | --- |
| `pybmap/transport.py` | Rewritten. Upstream uses `AF_BLUETOOTH` sockets (Linux) or IOBluetooth (macOS); Windows exposes Bluetooth only through Winsock, so this is a `ctypes` binding to `ws2_32.dll` using `AF_BTH` / `BTHPROTO_RFCOMM`. Byte-pipe semantics, error types and `errno` reporting are preserved so the channel-probing logic above it is unchanged. |
| `pybmap/discovery.py` | Rewritten. Upstream shells out to `bluetoothctl` and reads the device's `Modalias`. Windows has no equivalent, so the paired-device list comes from `BTHPORT\Parameters\Devices`, live state from `bluetoothapis.dll`, and the product ID from SetupAPI PnP hardware IDs. |
| `pybmap/messages.py` | Added. Localises the (deliberately unchanged) upstream error strings for the GUI and CLI. |
| `pybmap/__init__.py` | Adapted. Same `connect()` contract and the same channel-probing logic as upstream, with the transport factory and auto-detection swapped to the Windows implementations. |
| `pybmap/mock.py` | Added. An in-memory BMAP device so the GUI, CLI and tests run with no hardware. |
| `pybmap/devices/__init__.py` | One addition: the two QC35 product IDs (`0x400C`, `0x4020`) are registered so the legacy generation is auto-detected. Upstream left this as a `TODO`. |
| `gui/` | Added. The desktop front end (CustomTkinter). |
| `cli.py`, `bosectl.py` | Added. Windows console entry point and a unified dev entry point. |
| `build/` | Added. Icon generation, PyInstaller specs, Windows version resource. |
| `.github/workflows/` | Added. CI, packaging and release pipelines. |
| `docs/` | Added. |

